# Build context for the eastwood-core image (docker-compose: build ./eastwood-core).
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here lands in the image.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore uses Go filepath.Match, not gitignore semantics. A bare
# `__pycache__` matches only the context root. Use `**/` to match at any depth
# (Docker's `**` matches zero or more directories, so it covers the root too).

# Secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Private lead data — consumer PII must never reach an image layer
**/Leads_Export_*.csv
**/*.local.csv
**/data/private
**/exports/private

# Python bytecode, virtualenvs, packaging output
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/venv
**/*.egg-info

# Test and lint caches
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
**/htmlcov
**/coverage

# Git metadata
.git
.gitignore

# OS junk and logs
**/.DS_Store
**/._*
**/Thumbs.db
**/*.log
